From: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] shader_manager: build without OpenGL

shader.cpp compiles its OpenGL code only when C_OPENGL is set, but
ShaderManager calls Shader::BuildShaderProgram() and glDeleteProgram()
unconditionally, so -DOPT_OPENGL=OFF fails to link with an undefined
Shader::BuildShaderProgram (and glDeleteProgram would be a null glad
pointer at runtime). Guard both; without OpenGL a shader keeps only its
parsed info, which is all the non-GL renderer uses.

Signed-off-by: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
---
--- a/src/gui/render/shader_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/render/shader_manager.cpp
@@ -111,7 +111,9 @@
 		const auto& shader_key = descriptor.shader_name;
 		assert(shader_cache.contains(shader_key));
 
+#if C_OPENGL
 		glDeleteProgram(shader_cache[shader_key].program_object);
+#endif
 		shader_cache[shader_key] = shader;
 	};
 
@@ -181,10 +183,12 @@
 	               pragmas.output_size,
 	               pragmas.preset};
 
+#if C_OPENGL
 	if (!shader.BuildShaderProgram(shader_source)) {
 		LOG_ERR("RENDER: Error loading shader '%s'", shader_name.c_str());
 		return {};
 	}
+#endif
 	return shader;
 }
 
